    "author_association": "NONE",
    "body": "### Contributing guidelines\n\n- [x] I have read [CONTRIBUTING.md](https://github.com/nvim-mini/mini.nvim/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md)\n- [x] I have read [CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md](https://github.com/nvim-mini/mini.nvim/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md)\n\n### Module(s)\n\nmini.pick\n\n### Description\n\nI have a suggestion regarding the defaults for mini.pick\nIn the documentation mini.buffers has an example for adding mappings for deleting buffers. My issue is that deleting is not interactive if you have symbols enabled on deleting the symbol is gone but the name is still present we can provide this example instead.\n\n```lua\nvim.keymap.set('n', '<leader>bb', function()\n  local wipeout_cur = function()\n    buffer_items = MiniPick.get_picker_items()\n    get_matched_bufnr = MiniPick.get_picker_matches().current.bufnr\n    vim.api.nvim_buf_delete(get_matched_bufnr, {})\n    for i = 1, #buffer_items do\n      if buffer_items[i].bufnr == get_matched_bufnr then\n        table.remove(buffer_items, i)\n        break\n      end\n    end\n    MiniPick.set_picker_items(buffer_items)\n  end\n\n  local buffer_mappings = {\n    wipeout = {\n      char = '<C-d>',\n      func = wipeout_cur\n    },\n  }\n  MiniPick.builtin.buffers(local_opts, { mappings = buffer_mappings })\nend)\n```\n\nI can open a pull request if this suggestion looks valid to you.",
    "closed_at": null,
    "closed_by": null,
    "comment_data": [
        {
            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "Thanks for the suggestion!\n\n> My issue is that deleting is not interactive if you have symbols enabled on deleting the symbol is gone but the name is still present\n\nCould you please clarify what you mean by \"symbols enabled\" and how is it deleted but the name is present? Ideally, with screencast if possible, please.\n\n---\n\nOn the topic itself. The buffer deletion for `buffers` picker was discussed (at least) in #525. Since then I have been thinking of incorporating this action into the local picker (under `<C-d>` mapping by default, but configurable), just didn't reach the final conclusion yet.",
